WHAT THIS PROVES
The report was "the voice module is not able to set and start a route on its own, it says no route was
found". RoutesApi.fetchRoute is a blocking HttpURLConnection POST, and the spoken path called it from
`viewModelScope.launch` - Dispatchers.Main.immediate. On a device that is
NetworkOnMainThreadException, thrown *inside* the caller's `catch (e: Exception)`, which turned every
confirmed spoken destination into the spoken "Sorry, I couldn't calculate the route."

The throwaway test (app/src/androidTest/java/com/example/guidedogtest/RouteFetchThreadingTest.kt, since
deleted) made the route fetch from the main thread exactly as the voice path did, and was run twice on
the same device: A with fetchRoute as the plain blocking function it was, B with the dispatcher inside
it. The test source is identical in both runs - `runBlocking(Dispatchers.Main)` compiles against either
signature - so the only difference between A and B is where the fetch runs.

